WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.790
Everyone loves a good ghost story.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.680
Whether you’re crowded around a campfire
or watching a YouTube video at 3 AM, there’s

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.630
something fun and exciting about imagining
haunted places plagued by strange noises and

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.630
apparitions.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.580
Part of what makes it so fun is the idea that
any place can be haunted, especially if terrible

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.630
things have happened there.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.880
That decrepit old house at the end of your
street, that 80 year old movie theater where

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.600
no one goes anymore, a park where one too
many kids went missing.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.960
All it takes is a tragic backstory and a creepy
atmosphere, and it’s easy to believe that

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.080
any place could be teeming with restless spirits.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.480
So, it stands to reason that a place with
as many unsolved deaths as the SCP Foundation

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.350
might have a ghost or two lurking in the shadows.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:54.420
If you’ve ever suspected that the SCP foundation
might be haunted, well…you’d be right.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:01:02.100
It began, as all good ghost stories do, with
a series of frightening, unexplained events.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:07.909
Some time ago, personnel at SCP Foundation
Site-30 began to notice strange things happening

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:08.960
around the facility.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.140
Obviously, at a place like an SCP Foundation
Containment Site, strange is relative, but

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.060
these events seemed to have nothing to do
with any of the entities contained at the

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.060
site.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.560
There were unexplained sounds reported in
the private quarters of agents and researchers,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.190
ranging from whispers to screams from an unseen
being.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:33.990
Personnel who approached the D-Class block
at the site noticed an immediate drop in temperature,

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.950
with some employees even claiming that they
could see their own breath.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.990
Several personnel reported items going missing
while they were alone in a room.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:47.340
Most were small and easily misplaced objects
like pens and clipboards, but one man said

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.560
his wallet disappeared, which wouldn’t be
that strange if it hadn’t been securely

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.670
inside his lab coat.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:58.630
Other personnel would be innocently washing
their hands, only to be horrified by the appearance

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:04.009
of a bloody figure in a D-Class jumpsuit in
the mirror, staring back at them with hatred

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:05.009
in its eyes.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:09.629
There were anomalous computer server errors,
the feeling of being watched or followed by

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:15.650
some menacing invisible force, even the sight
of a shadowy silhouette fleeing down corridors

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.909
and hiding around corners.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:21.849
All of these occurrences were reported to
higher-ups at the Foundation, but they were

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:23.319
all dismissed.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:27.560
The Directorial Board of the site insisted
that these accounts were likely the result

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:33.620
of employees cracking under the mental stress
of working under such strenuous circumstances.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.749
If left alone, they were certain that the
reports would stop.

00:02:36.749 --> 00:02:42.300
But the reports didn’t stop, and they soon
found out that this was only the beginning.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.919
There was an uptick in containment breaches
following these initial reports.

00:02:45.919 --> 00:02:50.760
In total, twelve different entities were released
from their containment, and the origin of

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.250
these breaches could not be identified.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.480
Thankfully, the entities were captured and
returned to their containment facilities before

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.519
any casualties could result.

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:02.390
But from there things kept getting worse.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:07.669
Over the course of several months, there were
six different employee suicides on site.

00:03:07.669 --> 00:03:11.499
Security footage of the deceased operatives
shortly before their deaths showed them acting

00:03:11.499 --> 00:03:17.019
deeply troubled, engaging in agitated conversation
with someone not visible to the camera.

00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:21.949
At first, it was posited that whoever was
upsetting the employees was in a blind spot,

00:03:21.949 --> 00:03:26.379
but it quickly became clear that the dead
employees were being tormented by something

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:27.639
invisible.

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:32.920
Stories of hauntings were one thing, but now
with escaped SCPs and a notable death count,

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:37.699
the Directorial Board decided to mount an
official investigation into the unexplained

00:03:37.699 --> 00:03:38.699
occurrences.

00:03:38.699 --> 00:03:44.019
It was then that the spirit was officially
acknowledged, identified, and re-classified

00:03:44.019 --> 00:03:46.779
as SCP-4973.

00:03:46.779 --> 00:03:54.379
SCP-4973 was once a D-Class worker who was
used as a guinea pig in 25 different experiments

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:56.790
with a variety of entities on site.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:02.749
He was repeatedly exposed to multiple unusual
and dangerous anomalies, including SCP-158,

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:08.310
a large mechanical arm capable of extracting
an unidentified substance from any living

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.860
test subject.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:15.469
Before he was brought on board at SCP Foundation
Site-30, he was known as Gordon Kardivachlus

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:20.150
Markovitch, a man who had been convicted of
Murder in the Second Degree after stabbing

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:24.250
his wife 24 times in the chest with a kitchen
knife.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:29.570
During his incarceration, Markovitch was transferred
to the custody of the SCP Foundation and placed

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:34.890
at Site-30 where he was given a new name,
D-10000.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:40.050
During an experiment involving a redacted
entity, D-10000 was killed and his remains

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.440
were disposed of at a nearby waste refinery.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:47.540
It was then only three months after his death,
that the initial reports of ghost activity

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:48.890
began.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:54.950
SCP-4973 is regarded as a Class IV Spectral
Entity, meaning that it is an entity displaying

00:04:54.950 --> 00:05:00.090
a high degree of aggression and malevolence
toward a specific individual or group.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:07.450
In this case, the spirit displays hostility
towards a very specific group - the SCP Foundation.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:12.500
Class IV entities can affect the environment
around them, move objects, reduce the temperature

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.640
in a room, and induce hallucinations in humans
that it comes into contact with.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.480
These hallucinations are thought to be the
cause of the increase in employee suicides

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.560
that occurred after 4973’s first appearance.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.720
One of the many ways in which SCP-4973 acted
out, in what is believed to be an attempt

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:35.980
at revenge on the Foundation as a whole, was
to somehow gain access to the SCiPNET Database

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.040
Terminal.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.990
This allowed the spirit to learn about the
entities contained at the site, as well as

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:46.700
personal details regarding the lives of research,
security, and administrative staff working

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.700
there.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:53.390
This information is likely what allowed 4973
to cause several suspected containment breaches,

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:58.370
though the specifics of those breaches have
been expunged from official records.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:04.580
4973 was eventually contained within an apparatus
known as an Incorporeal Entity Vacuum Chamber,

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.990
which is consistently monitored by a team
of specialists within MTF Mu-13, affectionately

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.270
nicknamed “Ghostbusters.”

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:16.550
In order to prevent it from escaping, four
Harrington-Hollow Neutralizer Wards have been

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:19.340
placed at the door to the containment facility.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:23.570
This containment method has been largely effective,
though the spirit has escaped a handful of

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:27.800
times and had to be recaptured and placed
back into the IEVC.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:34.530
In order to understand SCP-4973, and uncover
how it was able to access the database, Dr.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:39.110
Lorraine Casper was assigned to conduct an
interview with the spirit, speaking to it

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:43.800
as it was in containment, and a transcript
of this interview is available in the official

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.400
Foundation archives.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:51.490
Dr. Casper began the conversation politely,
addressing the SCP as Gordon and asking him

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:52.710
how he was.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:57.370
Gordon refused to comply with the round of
questioning, going as far as to yell at Dr.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:02.270
Casper until she reminded him that he faced
the risk of termination if he refused to answer

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:03.400
her questions.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:08.810
Dr. Casper pointed out that the files accessed
by 4973 required clearance that the spirit

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.520
would have no way of possessing.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:15.380
He responded that he simply waved his hand
across the terminal in order to access it,

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:19.590
explaining: “It freaked out for a second
and then it just - stopped...

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:23.389
I could just move my fingers around the air
and the tabs would just roll up.

00:07:23.389 --> 00:07:24.389
Easy as that.”

00:07:24.389 --> 00:07:29.480
Dr. Casper asked for clarification, inquiring
how he could even do something like that.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.510
4973 continued his explanation, “Beats me.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.100
It felt like some attraction.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.720
Like magnets from afar getting closer and
closer.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.300
I dunno, something like that.”

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:44.300
Finding this answer unsatisfactory, Dr. Casper
pushed further, asking for an explanation

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:50.430
of SCP-4973’s attempts to release dangerous
onsite anomalies from containment.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:54.720
This question seemed to stump him, and he
claimed not to understand what Dr. Casper

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:55.720
meant.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:00.530
She explained that the ID cards of Dr. Yurkov
and Dr. Orson were used to open the facilities

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.220
from which these anomalies escaped.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:08.790
4973 was shocked that he had been suspected
of this attack, and insisted not to know who

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.300
Orson or Yurkov even were.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.060
All of a sudden, he trailed off.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.860
There was silence for a moment, and Dr. Casper
began to collect her notes and leave, assuming

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.790
that the interview was over.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:29.130
Much to her surprise, SCP-4973 began to laugh,
a loud uproarious laugh of complete and utter

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.130
delight.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:34.801
Casper asked what 4973 was laughing about,
and was met with the response: “God, this

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:38.019
whole time, you and your ghost-hunting crew
never knew?”

00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:43.060
He refused to clarify what it was exactly
the doctor and her crew had missed, only saying

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:47.080
“God, that look on your face when you find
out it’s been right under your noses this

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.080
whole time.”

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:53.060
He continued to laugh at Dr. Casper for the
remainder of the interview, refusing to answer

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:56.819
any further questions or explain any of his
comments.

00:08:56.819 --> 00:09:03.170
Finally, Dr. Casper grew exasperated and left,
ending the interview for real this time.

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:08.490
Following this perplexing interview, Dr. Casper
inexplicably abandoned her post at Site-30.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:12.959
Her supervisors could not reach her, neither
could any of the other researchers at the

00:09:12.959 --> 00:09:13.959
site.

00:09:13.959 --> 00:09:19.029
No one heard from her for an entire week,
until one day she called Director Eric Riverson

00:09:19.029 --> 00:09:21.810
of Site-30 on his personal phone line.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:27.220
He recorded the conversation, and a transcript
has been included in the file for SCP-4973.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:32.529
Dr. Casper explained to Director Riverson
that she had been hiding in her private residence

00:09:32.529 --> 00:09:37.220
away from the site, and that she no longer
considered any part of the site safe.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:43.190
In fact, she suggested that all SCP Foundation
sites might be potentially compromised.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:49.249
She explained her conversation with SCP-4973,
and the questions it provoked her to ask.

00:09:49.249 --> 00:09:53.529
If he had not been behind the containment
breaches, then who was?

00:09:53.529 --> 00:09:58.930
He never encountered Dr. Yurkov or Orson in
any of the tests administered on him, and

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:03.439
Orson wasn’t even employed at the Foundation
until after 4973’s death.

00:10:03.439 --> 00:10:09.069
Dr. Casper posited that, though the spirit
of Gordon was not responsible for the breaches,

00:10:09.069 --> 00:10:12.920
another spectral force, or forces, at the
site might be.

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.060
Her hypothesis?

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:18.890
That Site-30 was positively infested with
the vengeful spirits of Class D employees

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:22.180
lost over the years during various experiments.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:27.170
In order to prove her theory, Dr. Casper got
her hands on all of the experimental equipment

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:30.399
used by the department researching spectral
anomalies.

00:10:30.399 --> 00:10:34.759
The general consensus among researchers in
this field is that spirits leak out a kind

00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:38.649
of energy, known as ectoplasm, wherever they
go.

00:10:38.649 --> 00:10:43.940
It has been compared to the skin left behind
when a spider or a snake molts, a nonessential

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:48.790
portion of the entity that is shed and leaves
a residue in areas where they have been.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:53.889
Unsurprisingly, a huge amount of ectoplasm
was detected inside of Site-30.

00:10:53.889 --> 00:10:59.899
The spirits went undetected at first, as many
of them were dormant for quite some time.

00:10:59.899 --> 00:11:03.879
Dormant spirits are spirits that are not aware
of their surroundings or the circumstances

00:11:03.879 --> 00:11:08.379
of their deaths, and they do not emit large
quantities of ectoplasm.

00:11:08.379 --> 00:11:13.110
It is likely that, after Gordon was trapped,
several of the dormant spirits of Site-30

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:18.459
began to remember what was done to them, and
manifest in more aggressive ways.

00:11:18.459 --> 00:11:22.660
Because Gordon was presumed to be the only
spirit at the site, their gradual appearance

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:28.079
and acting out was either ignored, or presumed
to be Gordon escaping from containment.

00:11:28.079 --> 00:11:33.300
After her realization, Dr. Casper identified
an additional five active spirits at the site,

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.120
and was able to capture and contain one of
them.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:41.180
Dr. Casper warned Director Riverson that there
were likely far more spirits than just those

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:46.410
five, and it was only a matter of time before
they woke up and became active like the others.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:51.329
The large amount of previous containment breaches
attributed to simple “human error” becomes

00:11:51.329 --> 00:11:55.970
deeply sinister once it is clear that there
have been vengeful spirits hiding in plain

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:58.100
sight the entire time.

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:03.060
As Gordon put it in his interview, they were
just under their noses the whole time.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:09.079
Dr. Casper’s findings, and the story of
Site-30, present a troubling possibility.

00:12:09.079 --> 00:12:14.550
Every SCP Foundation site has used massive
amounts of Class D Personnel in human experiments

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:19.940
with dangerous entities, and the body count
at nearly all of them is staggering.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:25.839
If Dr. Casper is right, then every single
site has the makings of a haunted house.

00:12:25.839 --> 00:12:31.000
All of them could be infested with the spirits
of dead angry D-Class, who are just waiting

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:36.209
to wake up and take their revenge on the still
living members of the organization that killed

00:12:36.209 --> 00:12:37.209
them.

00:12:37.209 --> 00:12:42.569
And it’s only a matter of time before they
get the chance.

00:12:42.569 --> 00:12:49.939
Now check out “SCP-3999 - I Am At The Center
of Everything That Happens To Me” and “SCP-1007

00:12:49.939 --> 00:12:54.259
- Mr. Life and Mr. Death” for more mind
blowing SCP stories!

